Subject: refuse -H on VMS

VMS has no hard links that rsync could make: vms/vms_at.c makes linkat a
copy, which serves --link-dest but would make -H quietly give copies. D6
says -H is refused, so it is, before anything is sent.

--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -1241,6 +1241,9 @@
 #ifdef __VMS
 	/* VMS specifications among the operands, as paths (D5). */
 	vms_operands(argc, argv);
+	/* -H would give copies here, not links (vms/vms_at.c linkat): D6 */
+	if (opts.hard_links)
+		errx(ERR_SYNTAX, "-H (--hard-links) is not supported on VMS");
 #endif
 
 	if (argc < 2) {
